No shared memory by name (docs/gpu3d.md G1). ORC can link code for
another process through memory both map by a name - shm_open - and
Kosmos has no global names: a region is a capability handed to whoever
may map it. So that mapper is left out, as it is on Android, and says it
is unsupported; the JIT in its own process, which is what lavapipe is,
writes code into pages that are writable and then made executable,
never both at once (runtime/posix/mman.c).

